# Vakt frontdoor / reverse proxy.
#
# VAKT_DOMAIN controls certificate generation and HTTPS behavior:
#
# 1. VAKT_DOMAIN=vakt.example.com (production, recommended)
#    → Caddy obtains and auto-renews a Let's-Encrypt certificate
#    → Accessible via HTTPS from any browser without warnings
#    → Requires: public domain + ports 80/443 reachable from the internet
#
# 2. VAKT_DOMAIN=localhost (default, development only)
#    → Caddy serves HTTPS using its own INTERNAL CA (a locally-trusted cert,
#      not a "self-signed" one — the distinction matters: Caddy installs its
#      root into the local trust store, so localhost works without warnings)
#    → Safe for local testing only
#    → ⚠️  REMOTE TRAP: the site address below is a HOST MATCHER. With the
#       default it matches only the name "localhost", so a request to the
#       server's IP does not match this site at all. The symptom is NOT a
#       certificate warning you can click through — measured against caddy:2:
#         http://server-ip   → HTTP 200 with Content-Length: 0. A BLANK PAGE,
#                              no error, no status code to search for. This is
#                              the confusing one: nothing looks broken.
#         https://server-ip  → no certificate exists for that name, so the TLS
#                              handshake is aborted by the server (alert 80,
#                              "internal error"). The browser shows ERR_SSL_*;
#                              there is no "add exception" page to accept.
#       Always set a real domain for remote deployments.
#
# 3. VAKT_DOMAIN=:80 (behind your own TLS terminator)
#    → Caddy serves plain HTTP; upstream proxy (nginx, HAProxy, etc.)
#      handles HTTPS. Useful if you already have centralized TLS.
{$VAKT_DOMAIN:localhost} {
	# Backend API + health check → api service.
	# flush_interval -1 keeps SSE streams (AI chat, control explanations)
	# unbuffered so tokens arrive live.
	@api path /api/* /health
	handle @api {
		reverse_proxy api:8080 {
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}

	# Everything else → the self-serving frontend SPA image.
	handle {
		reverse_proxy frontend:80
	}
}
